cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "HRA-RLM: Hybrid Retrieval-Augmented Recursive Language Model"
authors:
  - name: "Sidra"
    alias: "Sidra-009"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Sidra-009/hybrid-retrieval-augmented-rlm"
abstract: >
  A retrieval-gated architecture that reduces token usage, inference cost,
  and latency of recursive LLM reasoning over long documents by selectively
  retrieving semantically relevant passages via HNSW before triggering
  recursion, benchmarked against a baseline recursive LM.
keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - recursive language models
  - HNSW
  - long-context reasoning
  - cost-efficient inference
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-09-14